Stage 4 — persistent database and storage: measurement transcript
=================================================================
2026-09-05, branch production-acceptance. Every path below is a throwaway
directory under /tmp created by `mktemp -d`; nothing here touched a real
database, a real storage root, or the repository's own prisma/dev.db.

$TMP = /tmp/pa-stage4-XXXX   (mktemp -d, removed after the run)

Prisma's per-migration progress lines are trimmed to the last few lines of each
command; two aborted attempts at the sqlite pragma probe (a shell quoting
mistake of mine, not product behaviour) are omitted. Exit codes are as reported
by the shell.

### 1. the exact command the container CMD runs, against an empty database
$ DATABASE_URL="file:$TMP/db/pdfdadi.db" \
    node node_modules/prisma/build/index.js migrate deploy --schema prisma/schema.prisma
  └─ 20260902100000_add_workspace_save_intents/
    └─ migration.sql
  └─ 20260905090000_add_instance_lease/
    └─ migration.sql

All migrations have been successfully applied.
exit=0

### 2. the same command again — a redeploy has to be a no-op
$ DATABASE_URL="file:$TMP/db/pdfdadi.db" \
    node node_modules/prisma/build/index.js migrate deploy --schema prisma/schema.prisma

No pending migrations to apply.
exit=0

### 3. what the deployed database looks like afterwards
$ node -e '<node:sqlite pragmas>' "$TMP/db/pdfdadi.db"
journal_mode       = delete
_prisma_migrations = 24 rows
tables             = 43
integrity_check    = ok
page_size/count    = 4096 / 234
$ ls -l $TMP/db
-rw-r--r--  1  958464  pdfdadi.db          # 234 x 4096 = 958464

### 4. local storage adapter round trip on a throwaway root
$ npx tsx /tmp/pa-storage-probe.mts "$TMP/storage"
put+get round trip:      PASS (38 bytes)
nested key created dirs: PASS $TMP/storage/documents/ab/cd/abcdef0123.pdf
file mode:               0644
traversal key refused:   PASS (Invalid storage key (escapes root): ../../es…)
delete removes the file: PASS
exit=0

### 5. a storage root that does not exist yet (a freshly attached empty volume)
$ npx tsx /tmp/pa-storage-probe.mts "$TMP/fresh-root/nested"
put+get round trip:      PASS (38 bytes)
nested key created dirs: PASS $TMP/fresh-root/nested/documents/ab/cd/abcdef0123.pdf
file mode:               0644
traversal key refused:   PASS (Invalid storage key (escapes root): ../../es…)
delete removes the file: PASS
exit=0

### 6. a DATABASE_URL that is absolute but points outside every mount
$ DATABASE_URL="file:$TMP/absent2/pdfdadi.db" \
    node node_modules/prisma/build/index.js migrate deploy --schema prisma/schema.prisma
All migrations have been successfully applied.
exit=0
$ ls -l $TMP/absent2
-rw-r--r--  1  958464  pdfdadi.db
migrations applied in the wrong-but-absolute location: 24

=> Prisma CREATES the directory. An absolute path with a typo in it boots
   healthy on a brand-new empty database; nothing in the process can tell that
   apart from a first deploy. See the Stage 4 note on mount verification.

### 7. backup and restore drill (full run in 06-migration-restore-drill.log)
$ node scripts/migration-restore-drill.mjs
MIGRATION + RESTORE DRILL — PASS 16/16
exit=0
